    "name": "ahu1_sat_stpt",
    "title": "AHU-1 Supply Air Temperature Setpoint",
    "description": "The task computes discharge air temperature setpoint and a dehumidification flag every 60 s. While AHU enable is false the setpoint is 55 F (285.93 K). On each rising edge of AHU enable start a 600 s pulldown timer that holds the setpoint at 55 F. After pulldown expires compute an outdoor reset: 65 F (291.48 K) when outdoor is at or below 60 F (288.71 K), 55 F when outdoor is at or above 70 F (294.26 K), linear in between with setpoint falling 1 F for each 1 F rise in outdoor. A dehumidification latch sets when return humidity stays above 0.60 for 300 s continuously and forces the setpoint to 55 F regardless of outdoor, and clears when humidity falls below 0.55 with control returning to outdoor reset. The dehumidification active output mirrors the latch. The document does not define start up values before the first update or failed sensor behavior.",
